# Form UI consistency (Mercato modules + shared form surfaces)

Use these rules when building or refactoring **backend forms**, **custom CrudForm fields**, and **CRM-style editors** so the UI stays aligned with **`CrudForm`** and avoids one-off “design system drift”.

**Platform references:** `packages/ui/AGENTS.md`, `packages/ui/src/backend/AGENTS.md`, root `AGENTS.md` (UI & HTTP sections).

**Scope:** These rules apply to **any** backend admin UI: app modules under `apps/mercato/src/modules/**/backend/**` **and** first-party **core** module pages under `packages/core/src/modules/**/backend/**` (for example procurement, customers, sales). Do not treat `packages/core/.../backend` as exempt from CrudForm parity or entity search patterns.

**Related Cursor rules:** `.cursor/rules/entity-search-combobox.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/detail-two-column-layout.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/module-backend-ui.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/association-link-open.mdc`.

## Control styling (parity with CrudForm)

- **Source of truth:** export and use **`CRUD_FORM_TEXT_INPUT_CLASS`**, **`CRUD_FORM_SELECT_CLASS`**, **`CRUD_FORM_TEXTAREA_CLASS`** from `@open-mercato/ui/backend/CrudForm` for native `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` in custom fields and embedded editors.
- **Do not** use long shadcn-style utility stacks on plain form controls (e.g. `shadow-sm`, `border-input`, `focus-visible:ring-*`, `ring-offset-2`) when the field should look like a standard Crud row — keep the same minimal pattern as built-in Crud inputs (`w-full h-9 rounded border px-2 text-sm` family).
- Prefer **native elements + Crud constants** over `@open-mercato/ui/primitives/input` for controls that must **match CrudForm** visually; use primitives where the design intentionally differs (dialogs, special widgets).
- Merge error / invalid states with `cn` / `cnTw` from `@open-mercato/shared/lib/utils` (e.g. `border-red-500`) without reintroducing heavy focus rings for parity fields.

## Labels and typography

- Field labels in custom blocks should match CrudForm’s label treatment: **`block text-sm font-medium`** on a native `<label>` (or equivalent), **not** `text-xs text-muted-foreground` label styling for primary field labels.
- **Section titles** come from **`CrudForm` `groups[].title`** (and optional `description`). Avoid duplicating a second “group subtitle” above the same field grid (e.g. drop redundant “vehicle / subject details” line when the group already describes the section).
- Intro / hint copy may stay as **`text-sm text-muted-foreground`** paragraphs where it is **explanatory**, not a substitute for a field label.

## Hints and `description`

- **`field.description`** on CrudForm fields is rendered **below** the control (after the field component). Prefer that for help text when it applies to the whole field.
- For **custom** widgets, place **inline hints under the control** (e.g. under `<select>`) when the hint refers to the control itself (“select insurer first…”), so the order is: **label → control → hint** — unless product copy explicitly requires otherwise.

## Conditional and dependent fields

- Show dependent controls only when the parent value requires them (e.g. financing only for **business** usage; leasing company only for **leasing** financing).
- When the parent value changes, **clear stale dependent values** in form state (e.g. switching away from business clears financing and leasing company; switching away from leasing clears leasing company) so saved payloads do not retain obsolete data.

## Relation / lookup fields (search + “add in new tab”)

- **System entities, dictionary-backed status fields (icon/color/label), forms vs detail preview vs inline:** see `.cursor/rules/entity-search-combobox.mdc`.
- For entity pickers that need **search** and an optional **create/manage** action, use **`EntitySearchCombobox`** from `@open-mercato/ui/backend/inputs/EntitySearchCombobox` (Popover + **cmdk**), not ad-hoc dropdowns, when the pattern is already adopted for that flow.
- The **square `+` control** opens **`window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer')`** — new tab for **create** or **settings** URLs configured per field (`createInNewTabHref` on Crud `select` when `useEntitySearchCombobox` is set, or props on custom usage).
- **Special case — “child” entity managed on parent:** e.g. **insurer contacts**: `+` should open the **selected parent’s** admin page (edit insurer) to add contacts, not a generic create URL when no parent is selected — hide or omit `+` until the parent is chosen if there is no valid target.

## CrudForm `select` + entity search

- Optional builtin flags (see `CrudForm` types): **`useEntitySearchCombobox`**, **`remoteSelectSearch`** (server refetch per query), **`createInNewTabHref`** (string or `(values) => string | undefined`), **`createInNewTabAriaLabel`**.
- Prefer **client-side filtering** on loaded options when the loader returns a full list; use **`remoteSelectSearch`** when the API is **search-driven** (e.g. unlinked leads with `search` query param).

## List APIs and filters (example: insurance leads)

- When combining **“only unlinked records”** with **text search**, express the search clause under **`$and`** (e.g. append `{ $or: [...] }` to `filter.$and`) so it **always ANDs** with `linkedPolicy: null` (or equivalent) — avoid ambiguous top-level `$or` that can weaken the unlinked constraint depending on ORM composition.

## Buttons

- Non-submit controls: **`type="button"`** explicitly; use **`Button`** / **`IconButton`** from UI primitives per `packages/ui/AGENTS.md` — no raw `<button>` for interactive controls.

## Detail grids (`DetailFieldsSection` + inline editors)

- **`DetailFieldsSection`** merges **`className`** with **`cn()`** / **tailwind-merge** — prefer overrides like **`md:grid-cols-2`** instead of duplicating the full grid class string.
- **Full-width field inside the default grid** (`grid-cols-1` / `sm:grid-cols-2` / `md:grid-cols-3`): set **`gridClassName: 'sm:col-span-2 md:col-span-3'`** on that **`DetailFieldConfig`** (e.g. a single multiline “Description” in a narrow sidebar). **Do not** move the whole section out of its column just to widen one control.
- **`InlineTextEditor`**, **`InlineSelectEditor`**, **`InlineMultilineEditor`** — **`variant="muted"`** uses **`border border-border bg-background p-3`** and **`overflow-hidden`** on the container so **text** and **select / entity search** preview tiles look identical; do not reintroduce **`bg-muted/20`** vs **`bg-muted/30`** splits between field kinds.
- **`InlineSelectEditor`**: use **`embedEditTriggerInDisplay={true}`** only when **`renderDisplay`** places the pencil with other corner actions (e.g. relations). Otherwise omit it (default **`false`**) so the **standard trailing pencil** shows on row hover like other inline fields.
- **Entity search trigger** styling inside inline edit: see **`.cursor/rules/entity-search-combobox.mdc`** (ghost + border + transparent fill).

**Detail page shell** (7fr/3fr, section cards): **`.cursor/rules/detail-two-column-layout.mdc`**.

## Create vs detail — same field type for long text

- When the **detail** screen edits a field with **`InlineMultilineEditor`** (Markdown preview + markdown editor), the **create** form for the same entity should use **`CrudForm`** **`type: 'richtext'`** (default **Markdown** path in `FieldControl`, not `textarea`) so users see the same editing experience and storage format.
- Use **`type: 'richtext'`** with **`editor: 'html'`** only when product explicitly wants HTML rich text instead of markdown.

## Module dialogs (tasks, suppliers, etc.)

- Put **linked entities** (supplier on a task, secondary lookups) **after** core scalar fields (title, body, dates, status, assignee) unless the flow requires the link first.
- Avoid redundant **hint paragraphs** under labels when the field is self-explanatory or behavior is obvious (e.g. do not duplicate “defaults to you” under assignee if the picker is clear).

## Relation previews (inline select + `renderDisplay`)

- For **corner actions** (edit pencil, “open in new tab”) on association previews, wrap the preview container with **`group`** and make the action row **`opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100`** (with **`pointer-events-none` / `group-hover:pointer-events-auto`**) so actions appear **on hover over the preview block**, not as always-on chrome.
